{
  "_comment": "The scene GameRules asks for when the last pickup is collected, and the other half of the scene-loading example. It holds ONE entity with one script on it: a scene does not have to be a level. Press Space here and WinScreen asks for collector.oscene, which unloads this one and starts the game again.",
  "_how_it_is_reached": "assets/scripts/GameRules.cpp calls eng::Engine::Get().RequestScene(\"scenes/you_win.oscene\"). Nothing in C++ knows this file exists - the name lives in a script, which is why adding a scene needs no engine change.",
  "camera": {
    "position": [
      0.0,
      0.0
    ],
    "zoom": 1.0
  },
  "entities": [
    {
      "components": [
        {
          "position": [
            0.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "rotation": 0.0,
          "scale": [
            1.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "type": "TransformComponent"
        },
        {
          "script": "WinScreen",
          "type": "ScriptComponent"
        }
      ],
      "name": "WinScreen"
    }
  ],
  "name": "YouWin"
}
